      "evidence": "The problem slide establishes time-cost urgency ('20+ hours/week') but does not name a budget owner or quantify the financial cost of inaction. For indie SaaS founders, tooling integration time has a direct opportunity cost (lost development hours, delayed feature shipping), but that cost is never stated. The common-mistakes criterion requires urgency, a budget owner, and the cost of inaction to pass.",
