      "status": "warn",
      "evidence": "The title slide positions Acmecorp as 'AI-native' but no slide in the deck substantiates this claim. The deck inventory records: 'Deck tagline states AI-native developer tools; no evidence of ML in value prop, inference/training in COGS, foundation-model mentions, or AI-specific retention metrics.' The traction claims ($8K MRR, 24 paying customers, 18% MoM growth) are stated plainly without hype. The AI label is the one unsubstantiated claim. YC partners have noted that unsubstantiated AI claims invite hard technical questions in the first meeting.",
      "notes": "Either remove 'AI-native' from the title slide tagline or add a slide showing specifically how AI is used in the product — what the model does, what data it processes, and what outcome it delivers that a non-AI CLI cannot match. A vague AI label with no backing is more damaging than no AI claim at all."
