      "status": "warn",
      "evidence": "The solution slide reads 'Acmecorp wraps GitHub, Linear, Stripe, and Vercel into one CLI' — a product description (form factor) rather than an outcome statement. The problem slide established '20+ hours/week' wasted, but the solution slide never closes that loop with a time-savings figure or a workflow outcome. Sequoia and YC flag feature-first framing as a common mistake; the solution should show the value delivered, not just the product architecture.",
      "notes": "Rewrite the solution slide around the outcome: how many hours per week does Acmecorp save? What does an indie SaaS founder stop doing, and what do they start doing instead? Lead with the outcome ('Cut integration overhead from 20+ hours to under 2 per week'), then show the CLI as the mechanism that delivers it."
