      "status": "fail",
      "evidence": "The deck makes no mention of compute costs, COGS, or gross margin trajectory. For a company positioning as 'AI-native,' a16z requires showing the path to 60%+ gross margins, including what drives the cost to serve (inference, API calls, hosting, support) and how that improves with scale. No such analysis appears in any of the six slides.",
      "notes": "Add a COGS breakdown or gross margin section showing your current margin, what drives the cost per customer (inference calls, third-party API costs, hosting, support), and the path to 60%+ gross margins as you scale. If your margins are already high (common for a CLI with no inference costs), state that explicitly — it is a strength."
