      "evidence": "The deck makes no mention of data privacy, secret handling (the CLI wraps Stripe and GitHub, which means it handles API keys), guardrails, monitoring, or compliance roadmap. a16z notes that for enterprise-facing AI products, addressing responsible AI practices reduces deal friction. No such mention appears in any of the six slides.",
      "notes": "Add a brief section (a few bullets on the ask or solution slide, or a dedicated slide) covering how you handle customer credentials and code (zero-retention of secrets, encryption at rest/in transit), what monitoring you run on CLI outputs, and your compliance roadmap (SOC2 timeline). This is especially important given that the CLI handles API keys for financial and code infrastructure."
